# tools/crypto_suite_witness.rish — the whole Season G crypto library, greened by one command. A choir that runs every per-file crypto
# witness in dependency order and refuses unless each prints its own GREEN line, so a keeper, CI, or the public seed can re-prove the entire
# Rye-native, parity-checked crypto stack — fifty primitives and twenty-four compositions, seventy-four files — without trusting any commit
# message (Season G · Cryptography · measurement beats memory). Fifty primitives and twenty-four compositions, seventy-four files.
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season G thread (Cryptography · Rye-native, Monocypher-parity, audit-ready).
# Design read: active-designing/20260815-175524_rye-first-crypto-parity-and-the-decision-wave.md (Season G · the crypto parity wave).
# Kin: every tools/crypto_<name>_witness.rish this choir runs; each builds its crypto/<name>.rye and asserts its GREEN crypto-<name> line.
# Monocypher (vendor/monocypher, CC0/BSD-dual) is the parity TARGET of the primitives beneath, never a copied line — our own Rye,
# studied clean-room (.claude/rules/gratitude-licenses.md).
#
# The order below is the dependency order the library was built in: the four hashes first, then the HMAC-SHA-512 and HMAC-SHA-256 keyed hashes and the
# HKDF-SHA-512 key-derivation function that stands on it, then the ChaCha/Poly stream-and-MAC line and
# their AEAD, then the Curve25519 base field and the edwards25519 curve (group, decode, scalar arithmetic, the two ladders, verify, sign),
# then X25519 key agreement, and last the three compositions (the signed carry, the sealed session, and the vault seal) that stand on the
# primitives above.
# Running a witness rebuilds its crypto/<name>.rye to the gitignored crypto/bin/ and runs its selftest, so this choir compiles and proves
# the whole stack fresh. Purely local — TEST keys and the RFC's public vectors, no real identity key, no network, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/crypto_suite_witness.rish

say "crypto-suite: Language EN — the whole Season G crypto library greened by one command: fifty Rye-native, parity-checked primitives and the twenty-four compositions that stand on them, each re-proven fresh from source in dependency order. This is the measurement-beats-memory capstone — every GREEN claim in crypto/ re-provable by tooling, not trusted from a commit message alone."
say "crypto-suite: Style Radiant — the order is the order the stack was built: the four hashes (SHA-512, BLAKE2b, the SHA3-256/512 Aurora names content with, and the SHA-256 Tablecloth keys content with), the HMAC-SHA-512 and HMAC-SHA-256 keyed hashes that stand on them, the HKDF-SHA-512 and HKDF-SHA-256 key-derivation functions that stand on those HMACs, and the Argon2 memory-hard password KDF that stands on BLAKE2b, and the PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA-256 iteration-hard password KDF that stands beside it, then the ChaCha/Poly stream-and-MAC line with its RFC 8439 AEAD and the XChaCha20 extended-nonce AEAD, then the base field and the edwards25519 curve, then X25519 key agreement and the birational Edwards↔Montgomery key conversion that unifies one identity across both, then the secp256k1 tower the Bitcoin/Ethereum world stands on — the base field, the group law, scalar multiplication, the scalar field modulo the group order n, the ECDSA verification that composes them all to check a Bitcoin/Ethereum signature, and the ECDSA signing that completes the scheme with a deterministic nonce byte-identical to Zig's — then the four compositions — the signed carry, the sealed session, the vault seal, and the Ethereum address with its EIP-55 checksum — then the ecrecover public-key recovery that reads the sender back out of a signature, the Ethereum account model's foundation, standing on the whole tower and the address it resolves to, then the SEC1 public-key serialization that dresses a derived point in its two canonical forms — the 33-byte compressed 0x02/0x03‖x and the 65-byte uncompressed 0x04‖x‖y — the rung every address and the coming BIP-32 hierarchical-deterministic keys reach for, then the EIP-191 personal_sign digest and signer recovery that authenticates a signed login — \"Sign in with Ethereum\" — end to end over the recovery and the address, and last the EIP-712 typed-structured-data digest that widens that authentication from a flat string to a tree of typed fields hashed against a domain separator — the permit / typed-login every wallet shows before it signs — then the EIP-155 legacy transaction digest that hashes the FLAT nine-field list [nonce, gasPrice, gas, to, value, data, chainId, 0, 0] a key signs before every on-chain send, folding the chain id into the preimage as replay protection and recovering the sender back through ecrecover, and last the EIP-1559 typed-transaction (type-2) digest that prepends the EIP-2718 type byte 0x02 to the RLP of [chainId, nonce, maxPriorityFeePerGas, maxFeePerGas, gasLimit, to, value, data, accessList] — the London fork's dynamic-fee default, its recovery bit a plain yParity because the chain id already lives inside the signed list — and last the BIP-32 hierarchical-deterministic keys that turn one seed into a whole tree of a wallet's keys, a child scalar (parse256(I_L) + k_par) mod n where I = HMAC-SHA-512(c_par, D) splits into the offset and the child chain code, serialized to its xprv/xpub text under Base58Check and proven against the spec's own published Test Vector 1, and the ML-KEM base ring — R_q = Z_q[X]/(X^256 + 1), q = 3329 — the first post-quantum rung, its modular arithmetic, forward and inverse NTT (FIPS 203), and NTT-domain multiply proven by self-consistency (the NTT round-trip and multiply-equal-to-schoolbook-negacyclic-convolution), and last the ML-KEM serialization rung standing on that ring — FIPS 203 ByteEncode/ByteDecode packing 256 d-bit coefficients into 32*d bytes LSB-first and reading them back, and Compress/Decompress rounding a coefficient into d bits and lifting it back — proven by the encode/decode round-trip over every width, the exact identity Compress_d(Decompress_d(y)) = y over every compression domain, and the FIPS 203 compression bound over the whole field — each rung standing on the GREEN rungs beneath it, none authoring cryptography a lower rung had not already proven."
say "crypto-suite: Lens TAME — each per-file witness rebuilds its crypto/<name>.rye and asserts its own GREEN crypto-<name> line against the RFC known-answers and Zig's independent std.crypto; this choir refuses whole the moment any one goes RED, naming the file that stopped it. Purely local — TEST keys and public RFC vectors, no real identity key, no network, no funds, no real device; constant-time timing-safety stays the Season's named horizon, and signing or agreeing with the maintainer's own identity key stays the custody gate."

# Dependency order: hashes, then the ChaCha/Poly line, then field/curve, then key agreement, then the two compositions.
let witnesses = [ "tools/crypto_sha512_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_blake2b_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_sha3_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_keccak256_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_shake_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_sha256_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_ripemd160_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_hmac_sha512_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_hmac_sha256_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_hkdf_sha512_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_hkdf_sha256_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_argon2_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_pbkdf2_sha256_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_pbkdf2_sha512_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_chacha20_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_poly1305_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_aead_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_xchacha20_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_fe25519_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_ed25519_group_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_ed25519_decode_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_ed25519_scalar_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_ed25519_scalarmul_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_ed25519_muladd_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_ed25519_verify_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_ed25519_sign_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_x25519_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_ed25519_to_x25519_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_fe_secp256k1_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_secp256k1_group_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_secp256k1_scalarmul_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_secp256k1_scalar_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_secp256k1_ecdsa_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_secp256k1_ecdsa_sign_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_signed_carry_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_sealed_session_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_vault_seal_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_eth_address_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_bitcoin_address_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_secp256k1_ecrecover_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_secp256k1_pubkey_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_eth_personal_sign_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_eip712_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_eip155_tx_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_eip1559_tx_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_bip32_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_bip39_seed_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_bip39_mnemonic_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_bip44_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_slip10_ed25519_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_kumara_path_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_kumara_identity_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_kumara_carry_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_kumara_subkey_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_kumara_attestation_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_kumara_sealed_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_verify_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_elligator_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_x25519_dirty_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_elligator_key_pair_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_mlkem_ring_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_mlkem_encode_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_mlkem_sample_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_mlkem_keygen_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_mlkem_encaps_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_mlkem_decaps_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_mldsa_ring_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_mldsa_encode_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_mldsa_sample_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_mldsa_keygen_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_mldsa_sign_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_mldsa_verify_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_mldsa_identity_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_mlkem_sealed_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_kumara_pq_identity_witness.rish" "tools/crypto_kumara_pq_sealed_witness.rish" ]

for-each witnesses as w do assert (run ["rishi/bin/rishi" "run" w]).ok else "crypto-suite: a per-file witness went RED — ${w}"

# The count-guard loom (REDS #80): assert the choir registers exactly the crypto/*.rye files on disk — a file and its proof can never
# disagree without this going RED, and the computed count it prints is the source of truth for the spelled numbers in the front-door docs.
assert (run ["rishi/bin/rishi" "run" "tools/crypto_count_guard_witness.rish"]).ok else "crypto-suite: the count guard went RED — a crypto/*.rye file and its suite registration disagree"

say "GREEN: crypto-suite — all seventy-four Season G crypto files (fifty primitives + twenty-four compositions) built fresh and proven, each its own GREEN line, in dependency order; the count guard confirms the file count"
